/**
@mainpage Overview

<div class="hero">
<span class="hero-title">llamad</span>
<span class="hero-tagline">One llama.cpp model, loaded once and served to every local application over gRPC on a
Unix domain socket. Generate stubs from one proto file, in any language, and get streaming chat, tool
calling, schema-constrained replies and embeddings.</span>
<span class="hero-links">@ref wire_protocol "Wire protocol" @ref md_docs_2protocol "Integration guide"
@ref architecture "Architecture"</span>
</div>

@section overview_quickstart Quick start

Start the daemon with any GGUF model, then call it. The daemon answers gRPC reflection, so grpcurl
needs no copy of the proto:

```sh
./build-cpu/llamad --model /absolute/path/to/model.gguf
# [llamad] listening on unix:/run/user/1000/llamad.sock

grpcurl -plaintext -d '{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Name three primes."}]}' \
    unix:///run/user/1000/llamad.sock llamad.v1.Llama/Chat
```

From an application, through stubs generated from `llamad.proto`:

```py
import grpc
from llamad.v1 import llamad_pb2 as pb, llamad_pb2_grpc as rpc   # generated from llamad.proto

stub = rpc.LlamaStub(grpc.insecure_channel("unix:/run/user/1000/llamad.sock"))
for chunk in stub.Chat(pb.ChatRequest(messages=[pb.ChatMessage(role="user", content="Hi")])):
    if chunk.WhichOneof("chunk") == "text":
        print(chunk.text, end="")
```

<a href="https://github.com/crybo-rybo/llamad/blob/main/docs/building.md">Building</a> covers
dependencies and GPU builds, and
<a href="https://github.com/crybo-rybo/llamad/blob/main/docs/daemon.md">running the daemon</a> covers
its flags, socket and signals.

@section overview_rpcs The service

| RPC | Request | Response | What it does |
|---|---|---|---|
| @ref wire_rpc_GetModelInfo "GetModelInfo" | @ref wire_GetModelInfoRequest "GetModelInfoRequest" | @ref wire_ModelInfo "ModelInfo" | Model metadata, without running it |
| @ref wire_rpc_Tokenize "Tokenize" | @ref wire_TokenizeRequest "TokenizeRequest" | @ref wire_TokenizeResponse "TokenizeResponse" | Text to token IDs |
| @ref wire_rpc_Generate "Generate" | @ref wire_GenerateRequest "GenerateRequest" | @ref wire_GenerateChunk "GenerateChunk" <span class="badge badge-stream">stream</span> | Completes a raw prompt |
| @ref wire_rpc_Chat "Chat" | @ref wire_ChatRequest "ChatRequest" | @ref wire_GenerateChunk "GenerateChunk" <span class="badge badge-stream">stream</span> | Chat through the model's template, with tools or a response schema |
| @ref wire_rpc_Embed "Embed" | @ref wire_EmbedRequest "EmbedRequest" | @ref wire_EmbedResponse "EmbedResponse" | One L2-normalised vector per input |

@section overview_contract The contract

<div class="cards">
<div class="card"><span class="card-title">A strict stream shape</span>
Zero or more `text` chunks, then exactly one `finish`, as a protobuf `oneof`. Text is user-visible
output only: never tool-call markup, never part of a stop string, never partial UTF-8.
</div>
<div class="card"><span class="card-title">Whole tool calls</span>
Calls arrive complete on `finish`, with JSON arguments constrained to the tool's schema, and only
when the finish reason is `TOOL_CALLS`.
</div>
<div class="card"><span class="card-title">Stateless requests</span>
Each request carries its whole conversation and its tools. The daemon never runs a tool and keeps
no sessions; the KV cache only makes a resent prefix cheaper.
</div>
<div class="card"><span class="card-title">Local only</span>
A Unix socket created 0600 and no TCP listener. Access control is the socket's file permissions.
</div>
</div>

@ref wire_guarantees "The guarantees in full" are written at the top of the proto.

@section overview_cpp The C++ API

Applications never link against these: the proto is the whole integration surface. The reference
is for working on the daemon itself.

<div class="cards">
<div class="card"><span class="card-title">@ref llamad::Engine "Engine"</span>
Loads the model and runs it over the public libllama API: tokenizing, sampling, streaming
generation and embeddings.
</div>
<div class="card"><span class="card-title">@ref llamad::ChatFormat "ChatFormat"</span>
Renders conversations and tools through the model's own Jinja template and parses tool calls out of
the generated text.
</div>
<div class="card"><span class="card-title">@ref llamad::LlamaService "LlamaService"</span>
The gRPC service: maps each RPC onto the engine and chat layer, and errors onto status codes.
</div>
<div class="card"><span class="card-title">@ref wire.h "llamad::wire"</span>
Field-by-field conversion between wire messages and plain engine types, and the `finish` chunk.
</div>
</div>
*/
